From: Gilly1970 <gilroyscott1970@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 21:00:00 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: npu: attach a coherent pool in the NPU window

The EN7581 NPU can only address host DRAM at 0x80000000-0xbfffffff;
higher addresses alias the lower 1 GiB. The coherent buffers allocated
on the NPU device are all shared with the NPU: the mailbox buffers
(with the coherent mailbox patch) and - since mt76 uses the NPU device
as dma_dev - the NPU TX/RX descriptor rings, the HW-RRO ba_bitmap/
addr_elem/msdu_pg/session buffers and the NPU TXD buffers. On a 2 GiB
board nothing keeps them below 0xc0000000; they normally land there
only because of early-boot allocation order. With low DRAM reserved
away on W1700K the SoC hangs right after mt7996 firmware load.

If the NPU node has an optional "dma" reserved-memory region, attach it
as the device coherent pool so all of these come from the window.

Unlike a restricted-dma-pool this leaves streaming mappings alone.
Packet buffers are passed through to the WiFi DMA engine: on W1700K
with 96% of TX skbs and ~20% of RX page_pool buffers above 0xc0000000,
host-path traffic and sha256 file round-trips stay intact, at the same
throughput as without a pool, whereas swiotlb bouncing costs ~22% of
host-path TX.

A device coherent pool has no fallback once full; mt76 and the mailbox
use ~10.7 MiB with MT7996, so the DT region should be 16 MiB.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Gilly1970 <gilroyscott1970@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_npu.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_npu.c
@@ -717,6 +717,11 @@
 	.disable_locking	= true,
 };
 
+static void airoha_npu_rmem_release(void *data)
+{
+	of_reserved_mem_device_release(data);
+}
+
 static int airoha_npu_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 {
 	struct device *dev = &pdev->dev;
@@ -800,6 +805,19 @@
 	if (err)
 		return err;
 
+	if (of_property_match_string(dev->of_node, "memory-region-names",
+				     "dma") >= 0) {
+		err = of_reserved_mem_device_init_by_name(dev, dev->of_node,
+							  "dma");
+		if (err)
+			return err;
+
+		err = devm_add_action_or_reset(dev, airoha_npu_rmem_release,
+					       dev);
+		if (err)
+			return err;
+	}
+
 	for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(npu->cores); i++) {
 		struct airoha_npu_core *core = &npu->cores[i];
 
